<title>USA: Biopharmaceutics sets reverse split.</title>
<headline>Biopharmaceutics sets reverse split.</headline>
<dateline>BELLPORT, N.Y. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biopharmaceutics Inc said Thursday that it has authorized a one-for-four reverse stock split which will become effective with trading commencing on Wednesday, June 25.</p>
<p>The company also said it has signed a formal agreement acquire Caribbean Medical Testing Center Inc for $7.5 million, of which $6 million will be cash and $1.5 million in a note.</p>
<p>Biopharmaceutics said it believes the reverse stock split and the projected earnings from an expected acquisiton will enable it to achieve a regional stock exchange listing.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
